            "description": "Reproduces **Figure 9** (KV cache size vs. quality) and **Table 1** (Mistral-7B on LongChat) of *CacheGen: KV Cache Compression and Streaming for Fast Large Language Model Serving* (Liu et al., SIGCOMM 2024), using the authors' code on one Chameleon GPU node.\n\n**How to run:** launch this artifact, open `cachegen_fig9_table1.ipynb`, and run the cells in order. The notebook:\n- reserves a bare-metal GPU node (any NVIDIA GPU with 16 GB or more; tested on V100 32GB at CHI@UC and P100 16GB at CHI@TACC);\n- installs the authors' environment and runs a 3-document smoke test, then the full run;\n- downloads the figure and table, and checks the paper's claims, printing PASS or FAIL for each.\n\nSetup takes about 30 minutes. The full 50-document run takes several hours; set `END = 20` for a shorter run.\n\n**Expected result:** CacheGen 173 MB vs. 8-bit quantization 587 MB at accuracy 1.00, a 3.4x reduction. The paper reports 176 vs. 622 MB, 3.5x.\n\nThe repository also includes:\n- our reimplementation of the paper's delta encoding (Section 5.2), which the released codec omits;\n- extensions: NarrativeQA and TriviaQA, and lower CacheGen levels.\n\nAll of our results and their analysis are in `reproduce-results/README.md`. Original code: https://github.com/UChi-JCL/CacheGen. Paper: https://doi.org/10.1145/3651890.3672274",
            "disambiguatingDescription": "CacheGen (SIGCOMM '24): reproduce Figure 9 and Table 1, KV cache compression for LLM serving, on one Chameleon GPU node.",
